      "text": "The bold casting of an epic adaptation—placing the actor embodying classical roles as Helen of Troy and Clytemnestra—ignited a backlash that drowns out the craft of adaptation. An attack on the right to creatively reinterpret shared stories overshadowed the auteur-filmmaker crafting a mythic epic's vision, turning the creative enterprise into a culture war that overshadows the craft of adaptation. The digital agora where craft battles are fought became a public debate over who owns the Western canon.",
